[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3306299786","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110626#issuecomment-3306299786","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110626","id":3306299786,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FEiGK","user":{"login":"lostminds","id":17763524,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzYzNTI0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17763524?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds","html_url":"https://github.com/lostminds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-18T08:42:42Z","updated_at":"2025-09-18T08:42:42Z","body":"In what situation are you trying to quit your app on iOS? As far as I know you're not really supposed to quit iOS apps based on user interactions or while they're active. Instead you just let the user leave the app using the normal iOS features and then have the OS decide if it should keep running in the background or be terminated based on your app configuration, or when the user terminates it manually from the iOS app switching interface. With that in mind this, could this be by design as it should not be used, rather than a bug?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3306299786/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3308354494","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110626#issuecomment-3308354494","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110626","id":3308354494,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FMXu-","user":{"login":"alakoring","id":12171257,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTcxMjU3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12171257?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alakoring","html_url":"https://github.com/alakoring","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alakoring/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alakoring/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alakoring/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alakoring/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alakoring/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alakoring/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alakoring/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alakoring/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alakoring/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-18T16:12:47Z","updated_at":"2025-09-18T16:12:47Z","body":"It looks like at one point using `exit()` would get your app rejected by App Store Review but I don’t see that in the current guidelines. (Most recent thing I can find is https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/how-killexit-ios-application-button-click-pardeep-chaudhary/ …) In my games, I suppress the Quit button. Quit or Exit is not something I’ve seen in other games, and the player can always use the home button or gesture.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3308354494/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3310235991","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110626#issuecomment-3310235991","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110626","id":3310235991,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FTjFX","user":{"login":"WLHQ","id":106452668,"node_id":"U_kgDOBlhWvA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106452668?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WLHQ","html_url":"https://github.com/WLHQ","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WLHQ/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WLHQ/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WLHQ/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WLHQ/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WLHQ/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WLHQ/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WLHQ/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WLHQ/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WLHQ/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-19T01:59:07Z","updated_at":"2025-09-19T02:04:30Z","body":"Why is this an issue? Apple clearly states that you cannot programmatically quit or close an app and it will end up being an AppStore Rejection. I can't see this being a valid issue at all. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3310235991/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3310272235","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110626#issuecomment-3310272235","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110626","id":3310272235,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FTr7r","user":{"login":"alakoring","id":12171257,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTcxMjU3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12171257?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alakoring","html_url":"https://github.com/alakoring","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alakoring/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alakoring/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alakoring/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alakoring/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alakoring/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alakoring/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alakoring/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alakoring/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alakoring/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-19T02:20:10Z","updated_at":"2025-09-19T02:20:10Z","body":"I agree this is not an important issue but I looked for where Apple says this and couldn't find it. Can you give a link? (I imagine that would make it easier for the team to close this.)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3310272235/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3310323177","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110626#issuecomment-3310323177","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110626","id":3310323177,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FT4Xp","user":{"login":"WLHQ","id":106452668,"node_id":"U_kgDOBlhWvA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106452668?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WLHQ","html_url":"https://github.com/WLHQ","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WLHQ/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WLHQ/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WLHQ/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WLHQ/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WLHQ/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WLHQ/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WLHQ/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WLHQ/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WLHQ/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-19T02:47:17Z","updated_at":"2025-09-19T02:47:17Z","body":"https://discussions.apple.com/thread/2087402\n\nThis might help but it looks like the current guidelines are vague about it more nowadays and that's why it's hard to find. I did come across that it comes across as a UX issue that force quitting an app may make it look like the app crashed. Why is that it literally looks like the same thing when an app actually crashes or is closed by the operating system so that's the most logical explanation.\n\nSo with that said rejection could still happen under performance & safety sections of the current guidelines. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3310323177/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3313684135","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110626#issuecomment-3313684135","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110626","id":3313684135,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Fgs6n","user":{"login":"lexum0","id":2546522,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NDY1MjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2546522?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lexum0","html_url":"https://github.com/lexum0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lexum0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lexum0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lexum0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lexum0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lexum0/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lexum0/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lexum0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lexum0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lexum0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-19T20:13:08Z","updated_at":"2025-09-19T20:13:08Z","body":"It has legitimate uses for testing, accelerating development and testing when dealing with things related to launch, app state (memory) or performance, benchmarking or tweaking launch tasks or simply testing initialization and state restoration. It helps quickly kill the process and start again (with 1 tap), or interrupt an incomplete implementation. It helps with DX (Developer Experience).\n\nIt's not meant to be used on the App Store, but used for developing. It's a tool, to efficiently test different aspects of the app. \nYou can very easily add a note like many other methods stating that it shouldn't be used in Release or simply when submitting to the App Store. \nYou can simply disable the method in the Release template like it is now (just enable it for Debug).\n\nRegardless of the App Store guideline or policy, I can call `exit(0)` on both Objective-C and Swift on iOS. It's not a private API. Godot engine should allow me to do this call.\n\nIt's like SwiftUI's Self._printChanges() API. It's not supposed to be used, but it's there to help you work and debug your app. It wasn't supposed to be public, but they left it so developers can easily test their code. It's not even documented, it's a private API. But it's there to facilitate your work.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2fab5b8a-eec6-4cbd-94f2-923b457c1cf9)\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0f22369b-4494-4cbf-9221-414f84146fb8)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3313684135/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3313780452","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110626#issuecomment-3313780452","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110626","id":3313780452,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FhEbk","user":{"login":"WLHQ","id":106452668,"node_id":"U_kgDOBlhWvA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106452668?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WLHQ","html_url":"https://github.com/WLHQ","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WLHQ/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WLHQ/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WLHQ/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WLHQ/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WLHQ/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WLHQ/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WLHQ/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WLHQ/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WLHQ/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-19T20:55:44Z","updated_at":"2025-09-19T20:55:44Z","body":"I would add if you are wanting terminate the app without waiting for the OS to do so there is a setting mind you, have to be in developer mode for this. It's called fast app termination and it will kill any apps that are side loaded for development purposes. This is a universal way to quickly terminate apps once you as the user forcibly close it during development. This prevents in cases where implementing this on the debug side it could potentially be released into production or be somehow misused so that's apple's implementation an answer to that problem. It also gives other developers that maintain engines & etc a way to do these things without having to maintain a hacky way of doing things.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3313780452/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3634194865","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110626#issuecomment-3634194865","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110626","id":3634194865,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7YnWmx","user":{"login":"limbonaut","id":2766569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NjY1Njk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2766569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/limbonaut","html_url":"https://github.com/limbonaut","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/limbonaut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/limbonaut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/limbonaut/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/limbonaut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/limbonaut/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/limbonaut/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/limbonaut/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/limbonaut/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/limbonaut/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-09T20:40:40Z","updated_at":"2025-12-09T20:40:40Z","body":"Just a tip. If you really need to quit the app, like in CI or tooling, you can use `OS.kill(OS.get_process_id())`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3634194865/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]